{"id":"2026-11-20-ELF","date":"2026-11-20","ticker":"ELF","name":"e.l.f. Beauty","sector":"Consumer Staples","industry":"Household & Personal Products","price":113.77,"price_date":"2026-11-18","timeframe_days":120,"headline":"Rhode keeps e.l.f. growing faster than beauty, and the stock is resting above its 50-day average","side":"long","timeframe":"3 to 4 months, through the February earnings report","thesis":"e.l.f. raised its full-year sales outlook twice in six months, from 12% to 14% growth up to 22% to 24%, and Rhode is now Sephora's top brand while sitting in only about 40% of its stores. The stock doubled since May, then spent six weeks moving sideways between about 109 and 119 while the 50-day average caught up, which is a calmer place to buy than the breakout. On management's adjusted earnings guide of $3.82 to $3.86 a share, the price is about 30 times this year's earnings for a company growing sales above 20%.","wrong_if":"A daily close under 101 would mean buyers gave up the November post-earnings low and the 50-day average together. The idea is also wrong if the February report cuts the second-half outlook of 7% to 10% growth, or if Rhode's reorders at Sephora slow after the Europe launch.","business":"e.l.f. Beauty sells low-priced makeup and skin care under the e.l.f. Cosmetics and e.l.f. SKIN names, plus three more brands it bought: Naturium (skin and body care), Well People (clean makeup) and Rhode, Hailey Bieber's skin care brand, bought in 2025. Most sales go through big retailers such as Target, Walmart, Ulta and Sephora, with a growing share sold online directly. The pitch is prestige-quality products at drugstore prices, launched fast and marketed heavily on social media.","segments_note":"The company reports two regions. The United States brought in $347M in the September quarter, up 25% from a year ago. International more than doubled to $174M, up 165%, because Rhode's Sephora launch across 19 European countries landed in the quarter. International is now a third of sales, up from about a sixth a year ago.","growth_note":"Sales grew 51% in the September quarter to $521M, the 31st quarter in a row of growth. About 16 points of that came from Rhode in the month before the deal's first anniversary, so the old business grew too, helped by lapping a weak quarter last year. Growth will slow sharply from here: management expects 7% to 10% in the second half once Rhode is in both years' numbers. Operating margin swings a lot quarter to quarter because of deal costs; it was 10.1% in September against 2.2% a year earlier.","commentary":[{"point":"Rhode is Sephora's number one brand in every market it sells in, with one of the highest repeat-purchase rates Sephora has seen.","speaker":"Tarang Amin, CEO","call":"Q2 FY27, Nov 4 2026"},{"point":"Rhode's Europe launch was the biggest launch Sephora has ever had there, second only to Rhode's own US launch.","speaker":"Mandy Fields, CFO","call":"Q2 FY27, Nov 4 2026"},{"point":"Rhode is still in only about 40% of Sephora's stores worldwide, so there is room to add doors.","speaker":"Tarang Amin, CEO","call":"Q2 FY27, Nov 4 2026"},{"point":"The second half should grow 7% to 10%, several times the beauty category's low single digits, with the March quarter weaker than December.","speaker":"Mandy Fields, CFO","call":"Q2 FY27, Nov 4 2026"},{"point":"About $52M of tariff refunds will be spent on marketing in the second half, which holds second-half profit margins to the low teens.","speaker":"Mandy Fields, CFO","call":"Q2 FY27, Nov 4 2026"},{"point":"The $1 price increase last year grew dollars but cost units; the company has since cut prices on about 10% of items and unit sales are recovering.","speaker":"Tarang Amin, CEO","call":"Q1 FY27, Aug 5 2026"},{"point":"e.l.f. Hair launched only at Target, and nearly half its buyers were new to the e.l.f. brand.","speaker":"Tarang Amin, CEO","call":"Q1 FY27, Aug 5 2026"},{"point":"The UK and Germany turned around after a new German retailer took the brand, and Brazil opens at Sephora.","speaker":"Tarang Amin, CEO","call":"Q1 FY27, Aug 5 2026"}],"technical_note":"The price is above a rising 50-day average (107.85) and well above the 200-day (83.01), and the 50-day has stayed above the 200-day since summer. Since mid-October the stock has traded in a range of about 109 to 119, with a spike to 123 on earnings day that sold off the same session. RSI is 52, so the November pullback cooled the stock off without breaking the trend. Over three months it beat the S&P 500 by 20 points and consumer staples by 7. Volume is running about 12% above normal.","valuation_note":"On reported (GAAP) earnings the trailing P/E is 78, right at its six-year median of 79, so the stock is not stretched against its own history even after the run. Reported earnings understate profit here because of deal and earnout costs; on management's adjusted EPS guide of $3.82 to $3.86 the multiple is about 30.","levels":{"entry_lo":108,"entry_hi":115,"stop":101,"target":138,"note":"Buy between 108 (near the 50-day average and the bottom of the range) and 115. The stop at 101 sits under the November 6 post-earnings low of 105 with about one daily range of room. The target of 138 is about 36 times adjusted EPS and gives roughly two dollars of upside for each dollar of risk from the posted price."},"risks":["Growth drops from 51% to 7% to 10% in the second half as Rhode laps its first year, and the market may sell the slowdown.","Heavy second-half marketing spend from the tariff refunds keeps margins in the low teens, so earnings may look soft even if sales hold.","Most of the momentum rests on one brand, Rhode, and one retailer, Sephora.","Tariff policy and price-sensitive shoppers at mass retailers could squeeze the core e.l.f. brand again.","The stock more than doubled in six months, so it can swing 5% in a day; the stop allows for about one such move."],"catalysts":["December-quarter report in early February 2027, the first quarter with Rhode in both years.","Rhode store additions inside Sephora beyond the current 40%, and new countries such as Brazil.","Holiday sell-through data from Target, Ulta and Sephora in January.","Further unit recovery on the core e.l.f. brand after the price cuts."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-18","adj_eps_name":null,"quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2023-12-31","rev":270.943,"gm":70.8,"om":11.8,"nm":9.9,"eps":0.46,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":84.9,"eps_yoy":35.3},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-03-31","rev":321.143,"gm":70.7,"om":5.3,"nm":4.5,"eps":0.25,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":71.4,"eps_yoy":-13.8},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2024-06-30","rev":324.477,"gm":71.3,"om":15.6,"nm":14.7,"eps":0.81,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":50.0,"eps_yoy":-12.9},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2024-09-30","rev":301.075,"gm":71.1,"om":9.3,"nm":6.3,"eps":0.33,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":39.7,"eps_yoy":-43.1},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2025Q3","end":"2024-12-31","rev":355.32,"gm":71.3,"om":9.9,"nm":4.9,"eps":0.3,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":31.1,"eps_yoy":-34.8},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q4","end":"2025-03-31","rev":332.645,"gm":71.3,"om":13.3,"nm":8.5,"eps":0.49,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":3.6,"eps_yoy":96.0},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2026Q1","end":"2025-06-30","rev":353.739,"gm":69.1,"om":13.8,"nm":9.4,"eps":0.58,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":9.0,"eps_yoy":-28.4},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2026Q2","end":"2025-09-30","rev":343.936,"gm":69.4,"om":2.2,"nm":0.9,"eps":0.05,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":14.2,"eps_yoy":-84.8},{"q":"Dec '25","id":"FY2026Q3","end":"2025-12-31","rev":489.505,"gm":71.0,"om":13.8,"nm":8.0,"eps":0.65,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":37.8,"eps_yoy":116.7},{"q":"Mar '26","id":"FY2026Q4","end":"2026-03-31","rev":449.292,"gm":72.7,"om":-11.2,"nm":-11.0,"eps":-0.82,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":35.1,"eps_yoy":-267.3},{"q":"Jun '26","id":"FY2027Q1","end":"2026-06-30","rev":479.373,"gm":83.2,"om":21.4,"nm":13.9,"eps":1.12,"adj_eps":null,"rev_yoy":35.5,"eps_yoy":93.